INSPECT:
-> length()
-> charAt()
-> isEmpty()
-> isBlank()

EXTRACT BY INDEX:
-> subString() - str.subString(0,4);
-> indexOf() - str.indexOf("s");

COMPARE:
-> equals() - str.equals(str1)
-> compareTo() - Check greater than or less than Ex: str.compareTo(str1)

FIND:
-> contains() - str.contains("@")
-> startsWith() - str.startsWith("Swapna")
-> endsWith() - str.endsWith(".com")

TRANSFORM:
-> trim() - It is used to trim the space,it removes only end spaces.
Ex: str="swapna "
str.trim()
-> strip() - It removes unwanted spaces give required spaces.
Ex: str="swapna  123 "
str.strip() -> "swapna 123"
-> concate() - str.concate("hello");
-> repeat() - str.repeat(3);

REPLACE:
-> replace()
Ex: str="swapna"
str.replace('a','o')
-> replaceAll() - 
-> replaceFirst

-> split() - str.split(",");
-> join() - str1.join("|",str2);
-> toCharArray() - Ex:char[] swap = "swapna" tocharArray();
-> valueOf()
-> matches() - It is prediction whether it is there or not
Ex: str.match([0-9])
-> formatted() - it checks the content is in grammatical format or not
Ex: format("Hi, swapna scored 88%");
